<title>USA: Science Applications says wins defense contract.</title>
<headline>Science Applications says wins defense contract.</headline>
<dateline>MCLEAN, Va 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Science Applications International Corp said on Monday it had won a defense contract worth a potential $250 million to support global U.S. defense communications.</p>
<p>It said it will provide software, data integration and engineering services under the contract awarded by the Defense Information Systems Agency for a global system &quot;that will allow U.S. warfighters to have information dominance on the battlefield.&quot;</p>
</text>
